    {
      "severity": "method-definition clarification",
      "finding": "Reported ambiguous counts 12/0/80 and 7 reproduce only when ambiguity requires BOTH parties present and more than one row on at least one side. If interpreted as every group with any D/R multiplicity, 2018 counts are 105 (2019) and 25 (2021), including respectively 25 and 18 single-sided groups. README/evidence should state the both-party condition explicitly. Pairable counts are unaffected."
    },
    {
      "severity": "wording precision",
      "finding": "The index file adds only pollsteridx at the schema level. It is not an exact string projection of the unindexed combined table: existing shared field serialization differs. This does not affect the separately verified 1613-row combined/standalone projection.",
      "shared_field_string_differences": {
        "Percentage_of_Vote_won_x": 2052,
        "numberSupport": 1
      },
      "detail": "2052 outcome-label strings differ with maximum float discrepancy 1.4210854715202004e-14; the sole numberSupport string difference is 0 versus -0 (numerically equal), at CSV line 14558. No substantive new record or observation ID is supplied by the index field."
    },
    {
      "severity": "scientific boundary",
      "finding": "The 467/1/2 figures count prepared rows with a unique source candidate-pair under the screening predicates; they are not verified distinct polls or source-independent observations. All matched source N values differ from prepared reported_n. Low match rates are not evidence of distinct cohorts."
    },
    {
      "severity": "chronology boundary",
      "finding": "Present Git metadata and file-tree identities support recorded versions/dates, not independently timestamped historical public retrieval. 2021 bytes cannot establish 2020 forecast-time availability or historical Tierney bytes. Generator revisions postdate the 2019 legacy table and do not establish its exact transformation."
    },
